<%# Port of `Hujah/form.js` response-vote buttons: pick the stance this reply is
    posted as. CSS-only (no Stimulus) — hidden radios + `peer-checked` styling.
    Defaults to the replier's existing vote on the parent. Values are the Hujah
    `vote` integer column: agree=1, neutral=2, disagree=3.
    Locals: form, parent.

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.2) — docs/design-system/components/voting/StancePicker.prompt.md:
    "three 48px stance buttons spread evenly under a small grey prompt". So the box is
    `w-12 h-12` (48px), NOT the 44px of a vote button in `_vote_bars` — the picker is a
    bigger target because it is the composer's primary control, and the two sizes are
    the design system's, not a copy-paste drift to be tidied away.

    The unchecked/checked pair mirrors VoteButton exactly — 2px stance border on white
    with a stance glyph, inverting to a solid stance fill with a white glyph — except
    that here the state is a real radio rather than a server round-trip, so the
    inversion is spelled with `peer-checked:`. Tailwind emits variant utilities after
    their bare counterparts, which is what lets `peer-checked:bg-<stance>` win over
    `bg-white` on the same element.

    It does not go through `ds_button_classes` for the same reason `_vote_bars` does not:
    every variant of that helper is a padded pill with a font size, and this is a fixed
    48px circle containing one 16px glyph. See the long note in `_vote_bars`.

    WHY THE COLOURS ARE SPELLED OUT AND NOT INTERPOLATED (a bug fix, Task 4.2): this
    partial used to build the checked fill by interpolating the stance name into
    `peer-checked:bg-` with an ERB output tag, and that class HAS NO RULE in the bundle.
    `@source inline(...)` safelists the BARE utilities — `bg-<stance>` exists,
    `peer-checked:bg-<stance>` never did, because a safelist entry generates the utility
    it names and not every variant of it, and Tailwind's scanner cannot see a class that
    ERB assembles at render time.

    NOTE the `<stance>` placeholders above and below: the scanner has no idea this is a
    comment, it reads the file as text, so writing a real class name in this prose would
    emit that class from the COMMENT and the spec below would pass on a partial that no
    longer spells it out. Same defect Task 1.1 fixed with `@source not "../../../docs"`.
    Never name a concrete utility in a comment that a nearby guard depends on. The two white halves of the inversion are literals, so
    `peer-checked:fill-white` and `peer-checked:text-white` DID compile: picking a stance
    turned the glyph white against a still-white circle and the button read as empty.
    Written out below, the scanner reads them as text and emits them.
    `spec/requests/stance_picker_spec.rb` asserts both halves — the markup and the rule.
    Interpolate a stance into a NEW prefix here and you are back to the same silence
    unless you safelist it.
%>
<%
  # One mapping, used twice: to look up the replier's existing vote on the parent and
  # to render the three radios. Two copies of "agree is 1" is one copy too many.
  stances = {
    "agree" => {value: 1, colours: "border-agree fill-agree text-agree peer-checked:bg-agree"},
    "neutral" => {value: 2, colours: "border-neutral fill-neutral text-neutral peer-checked:bg-neutral"},
    "disagree" => {value: 3, colours: "border-disagree fill-disagree text-disagree peer-checked:bg-disagree"}
  }
  default_value = stances.dig(parent.current_user_vote(logged_in: true, current_user_id: current_user.id), :value)
%>
<div class="bg-white mt-2 pt-1 pb-3">
  <small class="text-grey">Post this response hoojah as:</small>
  <div class="flex justify-around mt-2" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Response stance">
    <% stances.each do |stance, spec| %>
      <label class="cursor-pointer">
        <%= form.radio_button :vote, spec[:value],
              checked: (default_value == spec[:value]),
              class: "sr-only peer",
              aria: {label: stance.capitalize} %>
        <span class="w-12 h-12 rounded-full border-2 bg-white <%= spec[:colours] %> flex items-center justify-center shadow transition peer-checked:fill-white peer-checked:text-white">
          <%= stance_icon(stance, class: "w-4 h-4") %>
        </span>
      </label>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
